description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/patch-with-tools.ts, use the vacuousEditReason import that is already present but currently unused.

Commit 9267810 landed the import on line 33 without its call site, so `vacuousEditReason` is imported and never referenced. This single edit adds the call and makes the import live.

Make exactly ONE edit. The anchor occurs exactly once in the file; copy it verbatim:

// Stage the modified file into a mitosis dir for the cutover machinery.

Replace that single line with the following, which ends with that same comment line:

  // DETERMINISTIC VACUOUS-EDIT GATE, UNCONDITIONAL. The region-containment gate above
  // is skipped whenever the proposal names no region, which is 91-97% of proposals
  // (113 of 4,357 gaps carry a region; 93 of 1,050 open ones), leaving typecheck as the
  // only substantive check on a path that self-lands via the mitosis cutover. This
  // refuses only when EVERY added line is a declaration whose identifier is never used
  // in the result, so it judges the edit's own text rather than its responsiveness, and
  // being deterministic it cannot false-block under load. Same helper feature_compose
  // already uses. Evidence: 6dc2005 landed two declarations that nothing reads.
  {
    const vacuousReason = vacuousEditReason(baseContent, afterSrc);
    if (vacuousReason) {
      await resetTarget();
      return structuredError("vacuous_edit", {
        target_file: pointer.target_file,
        detail: vacuousReason,
        before_sha: beforeSha,
        after_sha: afterSha,
      });
    }
  }

// Stage the modified file into a mitosis dir for the cutover machinery.

SCOPE IS VERIFIED, so do not relocate this block. Everything it references is already in scope at that exact point, all inside resolvePatchWithTools which begins at line 553 and has no nested function boundary before the anchor: baseContent is declared at line 580, beforeSha at 581, resetTarget at 633, afterSrc at 1223, afterSha at 1224, and structuredError is a module-level function at line 116. Insert the block exactly where the anchor sits.

Change nothing else. Do not modify the import line, the region-containment block, the egress gate, or the staging code that follows.

